    "detailed_description": "<strong>Step into the concrete heart of the post-Soviet era in &quot;Doma&quot;</strong>. Delve deep into the architectural psyche of a bygone epoch, and craft iconic Soviet panel buildings block by meticulous block. <br><br><br><strong>You can build</strong> with 4 block versions and 2 gamemodes <br><br>        <strong>Gamemodes</strong> <br><br>                - Historical Mode: You build already existing series of panel buildings by using a layout we prepared for you. Try to get as accurate as you can!<br><br>                - Creative Mode: You build anything that comes to your mind. There are no limits!<br><br>        <strong>Blocks</strong> <br><br>                - II-35: Most popular basic Soviet era panel type. Nothing much about it. <br><br>                - P-101: Modernised panel type with a little mode designer solutions.<br><br>                - II-18: Modified II-35 version, ussually building up to 9 floors maximum.<br><br>                - KOPE: One of the latest panel versions, usually used in the high rise 9+ floor buildings. Also dark red tiles were used in here. <br><br><br>With every structure, you don't just build a building - you forge a piece of history. The houses you are going to build are already exsisting somewhere in the lost part of Belarus, Ukraine, Lithuania... Anywhere...",
